    "user_request_original": "Design a 21-layer defect-cavity bandpass filter using Ta2O5 and SiO2 on Fused Silica substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: Ta2O5(1)|SiO2(2)|Ta2O5(3)|SiO2(4)|Ta2O5(5)|SiO2(6)|Ta2O5(7)|SiO2(8)|Ta2O5(9)|SiO2(10)|Ta2O5(11-cavity)|SiO2(12)|Ta2O5(13)|SiO2(14)|Ta2O5(15)|SiO2(16)|Ta2O5(17)|SiO2(18)|Ta2O5(19)|SiO2(20)|Ta2O5(21). Initialize thicknesses from iteration_16 gradient_thickness_03 candidate: [250.456, 288.503, 233.021, 296.316, 233.533, 271.065, 152.587, 333.157, 113.740, 196.749, 529.185, 249.863, 114.912, 186.653, 166.195, 307.354, 107.020, 246.445, 160.804, 305.151, 238.675] nm. Apply sinusoidal perturbation with amplitude 3 nm and period spanning layers 5-13 to those layers only. Optimize all layer thicknesses with bounds 50-350 nm for non-cavity layers and 400-650 nm for cavity layer. Evaluate coherent TMM transmittance at normal incidence across 1400-1700 nm wavelength range. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
